# Box-side files are rsynced from a developer checkout (often Windows,
# core.autocrlf=true) to a Linux VPS and executed there. A CRLF shell script
# fails on `\r`; a CRLF systemd unit is rejected. Pin LF so a checkout can
# never turn the runbook into a broken script (PICKET P1 ruling R32).
*.sh                    text eol=lf
tools/picket/**         text eol=lf
collectors/base.py      text eol=lf
